            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for to go bankrupt, then the Portuguese for in debt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a aplicação",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a aplicação — \"the app, the application (software); the use\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Descarreguei uma aplicação para aprender línguas. I downloaded an app for learning languages."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In speech a app. Also the act of applying: a aplicação da lei."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aplicação is a learned borrowing from Latin applicātiō \"attachment, application\" (EtymDB), from applicāre \"to join to\", built on plicāre \"to fold\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
